# =============================================================================
# BYTE-PRESERVATION RULES (narrow, deliberate exception)
# =============================================================================
# These files participate in a SHA-256 byte-identity contract: the historical
# reproduction guard (scratchpad_historical_reproduction_guard.py) and the
# frozen snapshot evaluations/router_v2_historical_reproduction_
# snapshot_20260815.json hash their RAW BYTES and refuse to run on any mismatch.
#
# The repository has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on checkout.
# Without `-text` these files materialize with different bytes in a fresh
# checkout than the frozen snapshot expects, and the guard fails -- which is
# exactly what was observed at tag historical-reproduction-baseline-20260815's
# original target (see docs/migration/DECISION_LOG.md, D7/D8).
#
# `-text` disables ALL line-ending conversion in both directions, so what is
# committed is exactly what is checked out. This is deliberately scoped to the
# guard-hash-sensitive set only. It is NOT a general normalization policy, and
# `git add --renormalize` was NOT run.
#
# Evidence for each entry:
#   - the 5 .py files + the .zip are scratchpad_historical_reproduction_guard.py
#     REQUIRED_FILES
#   - both *_manifest.json files carry frozen hashes in
#     router_v2_historical_reproduction_snapshot_20260815.json, and the 820M
#     manifest is additionally passed as `extra_files` at run time
#
# 2026-08-21: repathed from their original flyff_farming_simulator/-prefixed
# locations to their current root-relative locations. The Phase-7 root
# collapse (and later cleanups) moved these files' real content without this
# section being updated, so `-text` was silently NOT applying to any of them
# (confirmed via `git check-attr text -- <path>` showing `text: auto`) --
# a real gap in this byte-preservation contract, found during root-cleanliness
# review, not merely a cosmetic staleness. See MISTAKES.md.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

